atorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{4}{3})=(-53.130\\,1…)^{∘}≈-{53.130}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{53.130}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{53.130}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}-{53.130}^{∘}={126.870}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-{53.130}^{∘},{126.870}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n-53.130\\cdot 126.870≈-6\\,741\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282683 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282684 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282685 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282686 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282687 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1041 "selection" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282683 13194139534213 true] [17592186282682 1110 #uuid "2de1b9ec-2ce3-5f43-aef0-d2d472c22c7d" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282683 1034 "-6\\,741" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282683 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282683 1111 #uuid "268946e7-5527-5a92-a28e-53fdc72568b9" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282684 1034 "-6\\,731" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282684 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282684 1111 #uuid "7a5de78d-8204-59b0-97b6-53f125f809c1" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282685 1034 "-6\\,631" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282685 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282685 1111 #uuid "7738e148-e6ef-532b-a769-a0c953fd2cdd" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282686 1034 "-6\\,851" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282686 1111 #uuid "0c9e7c40-836a-5dad-81aa-97c4e3cb76f8" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282687 1034 "-6\\,561" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282687 1111 #uuid "67c8944a-bc97-5cd9-8b49-1007571d465e" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282688 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282689 13194139534213 true] [17592186282688 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282691 13194139534213 true] [17592186282688 1089 "q-330708" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282688 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534213 true] [17592186282688 1100 "Find the two solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{8-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}=\\sqrt{8}$ for $0<x<2\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." 13194139534213 true] [17592186282688 1113 #uuid "f29a6dbd-b262-5fdc-930e-f2d2316607f9" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282688 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{8-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x} & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\ 8-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =8 \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't find an equivalent equation involving tangent, since this would lead to us dividing by $0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can instead find an equivalent equation using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=0\n$$\n\nIn this case, we can find the principal solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value lies inside the desired domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nTo find more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}+\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, our solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282689 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282690 13194139534213 true] [17592186282689 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534213 true] [17592186282689 1041 "field-1" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282689 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282690 13194139534213 true] [17592186282689 1110 #uuid "94902314-a3df-52b9-8de1-513711ccceec" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282690 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282690 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282690 1111 #uuid "3a33c542-bcce-5088-aa86-76ed383a760b" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282691 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282692 13194139534213 true] [17592186282691 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534213 true] [17592186282691 1041 "field-2" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282691 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282692 13194139534213 true] [17592186282691 1110 #uuid "d65bd88b-96d1-5564-b9d4-1fd3cb386455" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282692 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282692 1111 #uuid "9373aa94-e594-5875-840b-af112ff604a6" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282693 1017 #edb/ref 17592186282694 13194139534213 true] [17592186282693 1089 "q-76930" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282693 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534213 true] [17592186282693 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{5}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282693 1113 #uuid "5ccb0e75-04a0-58e0-9f38-1667d6f95491" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282693 1145 "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=5\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(5)=1.373\\,400…≈1.373\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1.373\\,4$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.373\\,4.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi +1.373\\,4=4.515\\,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n1.373\\,4\\cdot 4.515\\,0≈6.2\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282695 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282696 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282697 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282698 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1000 #edb/ref 17592186282699 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1041 "selection" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1104 #edb/ref 17592186282697 13194139534213 true] [17592186282694 1110 #uuid "9b576ac6-7d2d-5d8b-a5e0-a730d875bb02" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282695 1034 "5.8" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282695 1111 #uuid "36d35d45-42ed-52cb-bd79-633b935f1cb5" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282696 1034 "5.9" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282696 1111 #uuid "9fdaf85f-52f4-5772-b936-fa11de57bf3a" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282697 1034 "6.2" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282697 1111 #uuid "5952884d-c0bc-5192-91c3-3262c4e76705" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282698 1034 "6.8" 13194139534213 true] [17592186282698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534213 true] [17592186282698 1111 #uuid "4493d027-4c78-5dc8-a9f9-908208ae85a2" 13194139534213 tr